.SS v21.7.8 (2026\-09\-01)
.SS Bugfixes \- 21.7.8
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
A missing source needed by both install modes now disables the builtin creator through \fBmeta.error\fP\&. The check
compared \fBRefWhen\fP values against \fBRefMust\fP members, so creation went on to fail with a \fBFileNotFoundError\fP or a
dangling symlink \- by @darrenhuai \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:darrenhuai>\&. (#3227 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pypa/\:virtualenv/\:issues/\:3227>)
.UNINDENT
.SS v21.7.7 (2026\-08\-28)
.SS Bugfixes \- 21.7.7
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Bump the \fBpython\-discovery\fP minimum to \fB>=1.6\fP for \fBPythonInfo.system_exe\fP, which reports the system interpreter
without the nullable typing of \fBsystem_executable\fP \- by @gaborbernat \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:gaborbernat>\&. (#3224 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pypa/\:virtualenv/\:issues/\:3224>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Improved Documentation \- 21.7.7
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Document the names the interpreter answers to inside a created environment. A new Environment layout \%<>
page lists them per platform, the tutorial and the usage guide point at it, and the explanation of creators covers why
an environment carries several names and why Windows copies a redirector \- by @gaborbernat \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:gaborbernat>\&. (#3225 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pypa/\:virtualenv/\:issues/\:3225>)
.UNINDENT
.SS v21.7.6 (2026\-08\-28)
.SS Bugfixes \- 21.7.6
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
On Windows, \fBvirtualenv\fP no longer copies the CPython 3.13+ \fBvenvlauncher.exe\fP shim into \fBScripts\fP under the
shim\(aqs own name, and a host such as \fBpython_d.exe\fP gets its alias back. The alias set took its names from the shim
that stands in for the interpreter, so every environment gained a stray launcher copy and lost the interpreter\(aqs own
file name \- by @darrenhuai \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:darrenhuai>\&. (#3223 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pypa/\:virtualenv/\:issues/\:3223>)
.UNINDENT
.SS v21.7.5 (2026\-08\-25)
.SS Bugfixes \- 21.7.5
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix the type check against \fBpython\-discovery\fP 1.5.2, whose annotations allow a \fBNone\fP \fBprefix\fP and integer
\fBsysconfig_vars\fP values: config var substitution now skips a missing prefix and locating the shared libpython
requires string \fBINSTSONAME\fP/\fBLIBDIR\fP values. (#3211 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pypa/\:virtualenv/\:issues/\:3211>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBExePathRef.can_run\fP now checks the group and other execute bits instead of only the owner one, and returns
\fBFalse\fP rather than \fBNone\fP when a file carries none of the three \- by @darrenhuai \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:darrenhuai>\&. (#3217 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pypa/\:virtualenv/\:issues/\:3217>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsafe_delete\fP no longer passes \fBignore_errors=True\fP to \fBshutil.rmtree\fP, which replaced its own chmod\-and\-retry
handler with a no\-op and swallowed every failure. Read\-only files \- every file in a wheel image, which \fBset_tree\fP
marks \- survived, so \fB\-\-reset\-app\-data\fP and \fB\-\-clear\fP kept trees they reported deleting. The handler now retries
only the deletion itself, keeps the other mode bits, and raises the original error for anything it cannot clear \- by
@darrenhuai \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:darrenhuai>\&. (#3222 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pypa/\:virtualenv/\:issues/\:3222>)
.UNINDENT
