.SS v21.6.1 (2026\-07\-10)
.SS Bugfixes \- 21.6.1
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Harden the fish activator prompt against user functions that shadow builtins. Routing \fBfunctions\fP, \fBprintf\fP,
\fBstring\fP, \fBecho\fP and \fBsource\fP/\fB\&.\fP through \fBbuiltin\fP stops a shadowing function (such as a dot\-style
directory navigator that redefines \fB\&.\fP) from hijacking the prompt and dropping the previous command\(aqs exit status,
matching the CPython fix in gh\-140006 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:python/\:cpython/\:issues/\:140006>\&. (#3185 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pypa/\:virtualenv/\:issues/\:3185>)
.UNINDENT
.SS v21.6.0 (2026\-07\-06)
.SS Features \- 21.6.0
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Stop installing the \fB_virtualenv.{py,pth}\fP distutils import hook for Python 3.10 and later, where pip, setuptools
and CPython already ignore the install config keys it guards against; this removes the hook\(aqs startup import cost. The
hook is still installed for Python 3.9 \- #3181 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pypa/\:virtualenv/\:issues/\:3181>\&. (#3181 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pypa/\:virtualenv/\:issues/\:3181>)
