.SS v20.10.0 (2021\-11\-01)
.SS Features \- 20.10.0
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
If a \fB\(dqvenv\(dq\fP install scheme exists in \fBsysconfig\fP, virtualenv now uses it to create new virtual environments.
This allows Python distributors, such as Fedora, to patch/replace the default install scheme without affecting the
paths in new virtual environments. A similar technique was proposed to Python, for the venv module \%<https://\:bugs\:.python\:.org/\:issue45413> \- by \fBhroncok\fP (#2208 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pypa/\:virtualenv/\:issues/\:2208>)
.IP \(bu 2
The activated virtualenv prompt is now always wrapped in parentheses. This affects venvs created with the \fB\-\-prompt\fP
attribute, and matches virtualenv\(aqs behavior on par with venv. (#2224 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pypa/\:virtualenv/\:issues/\:2224>)
.UNINDENT
